re is no Samurai Archery catalog row, so that trade is prose in the W.P. Archery note. || RELATED: six, plus one at levels 3, 6, 9 and 12. Science Astronomy and Mathematics only, read as Astronomy and both Mathematics rows. || SECONDARY: the book prints three secondary skills at levels 1, 4, 8 and 12, read as three at each of those levels (the same reading the other Japan drafts give this sentence). || BIONICS: the four bionic features and up to five cybernetic implants are a player''s choice from two books, with no key to grant them; they are prose abilities. || EQUIPMENT: the book''s first armor is a high-tech Samurai mega-damage body armor of 1D6x10+60 M.D.C., which no catalog row covers (samurai-armor is the True Samurai''s magic armor); the choice offers the samurai-styled HA-5 and HA-7 first and then other Japan armor, per the book''s ''or one of the other types of armor available in Japan''. Ten high-tech arrows of choice are one choice of arrowhead type, quantity 10. The energy weapon of choice is offered from the Japan pistols and rifles. 1D4 E-clips as the generic e-clip row, since the matching pistol or rifle clip depends on the weapon. Two vibro-blades or ancient weapons as a choose-2. The S.D.C. daisho is daisho-rifts. Transportation: horse, hovercycle or jet pack as a choice; the robot horse and motorcycle have no catalog rows and are prose. Ammo pouches are in the utility belt note. Money: 2D6x1000 credits stored; the Black Market items and the monthly salary are prose."
